# 4. FLAGSHIP FEATURE — MY SCHOOL DAY

The most distinctive feature of MERI SCHOOL DIARY must be the **My School Day** timeline.

Do not treat this as an ordinary timetable.

### Timetable vs My School Day

Timetable = What was planned to happen.

My School Day = What actually happened.

These must be separate features.

### Example

A school day may look like this:

08:00 – 08:40 | English
Teacher recorded: Chapter 4 reading and vocabulary.

08:40 – 09:20 | Mathematics
Teacher recorded: Fractions exercises completed.

09:20 – 10:00 | Science
No update recorded.

10:00 – 10:20 | Break

10:20 – 11:00 | Computer Education
Substitute teacher recorded: Introduction to computer networks.

11:00 – 11:40 | Urdu
Teacher recorded: Essay writing practice.

End of Day:
Students completed assigned classwork and received Mathematics homework.

### Timeline UI Requirements

- Vertical timeline.
- Clear time labels.
- Subject icons or simple visual markers.
- Teacher name.
- Period update content.
- Missing update indicators.
- Substitute teacher labels.
- Edited/backdated indicators.
- End-of-day report section.
- Date navigation.
- Today and previous-day views.
- Responsive layout.

The timeline must visually stand out from other dashboard modules.

