# 5. SCHOOL STRUCTURE AND DATA RELATIONSHIPS

Use a clean domain model.

### Main Entities

1. School
2. AcademicYear
3. SchoolClass
4. Section
5. Student
6. Guardian
7. Teacher
8. Subject
9. TeacherAssignment
10. SchoolCalendarEvent
11. TimetableSlot
12. AttendanceRecord
13. HomeworkItem
14. HomeworkSubmission
15. TimelineUpdate
16. EndOfDayReport
17. Test
18. TestResult
19. LeaveApplication
20. Announcement
21. DemoUser / DemoSession

### Relationship Rules

- One school can have multiple academic years.
- One class can contain multiple sections.
- One section belongs to one class.
- One section can contain multiple students.
- One guardian can be linked to multiple students.
- A student belongs to one section.
- Teachers can teach multiple subjects and sections.
- A teacher assignment connects one teacher, one subject, and one section.
- Students have individual attendance, homework, results, and leave records.
- Calendar events are school-wide.

Use stable string IDs and consistent relationships.

Do not duplicate class information on Student when it can be derived from Section.

### Unique Constraints

- Student admission number must be unique.
- Student roll number must be unique within its section.
- A student should not have duplicate daily attendance records.
- Avoid duplicate teacher-subject-section assignments.
- Prevent duplicate leave applications for overlapping dates where applicable.
- Only one academic year can be current.

