The initial application must work completely offline.

### Local Persistence

Use SharedPreferencesAsync with a schema-versioned JSON snapshot for the school dataset.

Storage key:

app.school_data.v1

Requirements:

- Seed data loads on first launch.
- Changes survive browser refresh.
- Data can be reset to original demo values.
- Corrupt or unsupported snapshots should safely fall back to seed data.
- Keep storage logic separate from UI.
- Use a codec for serialization and deserialization.
- Provide clean repository interfaces so a backend can be introduced in a future version.

Use storage compatible with Flutter Web and Android.

### Demo Session

- Local role selection.
- No email/password.
